{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The Claude refresh adapter is named refresh, invokes as /spec:refresh, and reloads one explicitly selected STDO registry entry. Its argument interface is (--installed | --release <product-local-cut> | --candidate) [--doc <name>] [--list]. Model invocation is disabled.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 5,
          "quote": "name: refresh\ndescription: Reload one explicitly selected STDO registry entry into context\nargument-hint: \"(--installed | --release <product-local-cut> | --candidate) [--doc <name>] [--list]\"\ndisable-model-invocation: true",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/claude-skills/refresh/SKILL.md#preamble",
          "start_line": 2
        },
        {
          "end_line": 15,
          "quote": "Claude invocation is `/spec:refresh`. This adapter adds no procedure or\nauthority and remains manual-only because a full registry entry materially\nexpands context.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/claude-skills/refresh/SKILL.md#STDO%20Refresh%20For%20Claude",
          "start_line": 13
        }
      ],
      "key": "claude_refresh_adapter",
      "label": "Claude refresh adapter"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Using STDO is a practical entrypoint for people and LLMs entering STDO-governed projects, addressing preparation, requirement iteration, authorization for code and tests, and monitoring and triage. It and its companion skills are non-deciding interaction projections; the exact installed STDO cut and Product-owned authority remain governing.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 13,
          "quote": "This guide and its companion skills are non-deciding interaction projections.\nThe project's exact installed STDO cut and Product-owned authority remain the\ngoverning sources.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO",
          "start_line": 11
        }
      ],
      "key": "using_stdo_guide",
      "label": "Using STDO guide"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The guide's contents provide navigation to Get Ready To Work, Iterate Requirements, Start Code Development And Testing, Monitor And Help Triage, Common Stops, and Owning References. These are document routes, not execution or authority.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 22,
          "quote": "- [Get Ready To Work](#1-get-ready-to-work)\n- [Iterate Requirements](#2-iterate-requirements)\n- [Start Code Development And Testing](#3-start-code-development-and-testing)\n- [Monitor And Help Triage](#4-monitor-and-help-triage)\n- [Common Stops](#common-stops)\n- [Owning References](#owning-references)",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2FContents",
          "start_line": 17
        }
      ],
      "key": "guide_contents",
      "label": "Guide contents"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Get Ready To Work is the guide's preparation section, organizing the supplied existing-project, plugin-copy verification, new-project, and shared-skills subsections.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 54,
          "quote": "## 1. Get Ready To Work",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F1.%20Get%20Ready%20To%20Work",
          "start_line": 54
        }
      ],
      "key": "guide_preparation",
      "label": "Get Ready To Work"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The guide distinguishes an immutable cut defining the selected method; stdo_<label>.json selecting it and locating Product authority, realization and work carriers; project-owned Goals, Intent, Product, requirements, design, code, tickets, decisions and evidence; and skills routing requests without becoming another method, workflow engine, prompt engine or source of truth. Its operating sequence is request, basis/outcome verification, triage and smallest carrier with admitted run contract, first-changed-layer re-entry, required truth/design update, authorized code/tests, exact candidate, required independent review, Product-owned disposition/checkpoint, then status/evidence/next authorized action.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 34,
          "quote": "- an immutable STDO cut defines the selected method;\n- `stdo_<label>.json` selects that cut and locates the Product's actual\n  authority, realization, and work carriers;\n- the project owns its Goals, Intent, Product, requirements, design, code,\n  tickets, decisions, and evidence; and\n- skills route common requests without becoming another method, workflow\n  engine, prompt engine, or source of truth.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2FThe%20Operating%20Loop",
          "start_line": 28
        }
      ],
      "key": "guide_operating_loop",
      "label": "Guide operating loop"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "New-project setup selects an immutable product-local cut and qualified repository ref, obtains a sufficiently recent toolchain, installs and verifies the cut, copies Product Definition and Project Reference-Frame Basis templates from that same cut, binds the project, obtains Product-owner ratification, and previews then installs only marker-owned bootstrap material. The displayed release values are placeholders bound at coordinated publication, not actual selected releases.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 133,
          "quote": "Select one immutable product-local cut and its qualified repository ref. For\nthe coordinated STDO distribution after publication, with every value below\nbound at its RC cut under `RELEASE.md` sections 6 and 7:",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F1.%20Get%20Ready%20To%20Work%2FNew%20Project",
          "start_line": 131
        }
      ],
      "key": "guide_new_project_setup",
      "label": "New-project setup"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The guide's change classes map current bounded work-wave focus changes to goal_reprice/Goals; direction or scope changes to intent_reprice/Intent; changed current product realisation with stable direction to product_reprice/Product; changed constitutional truth with stable project direction to requirement_reprice/Requirements; changed realisation structure with stable active intent and requirement truth to design_reframe/Design; and local code, configuration or attribute changes without intended constitutional or structural change to realization_refactor/the realised surface, requiring proof of no upstream drift.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 412,
          "quote": "| current bounded work-wave focus changes | `goal_reprice` | Goals |\n| directional or scope change | `intent_reprice` | Intent |\n| current product realisation changes while directional intent stays stable | `product_reprice` | Product |\n| constitutional truth changes while project direction stays stable | `requirement_reprice` | Requirements |\n| realisation structure changes while active intent and requirement truth stay stable | `design_reframe` | Design |\n| local code, configuration or attribute change with no intended constitutional or structural change; it must prove no upstream drift | `realization_refactor` | the realised surface only |",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2F2.%20Iterate%20Requirements%2FFind%20The%20First%20Changed%20Layer",
          "start_line": 407
        }
      ],
      "key": "guide_change_classes",
      "label": "Guide change classes"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The guide identifies owning references: SPEC_METHOD for the constitutional chain, triage, requirements, construction and proportional delivery; ACTIVATION for bounded construction and proportionality; ASSURANCE for testing; TICKETS for carriers, fields, states, contracts, test authority and projection; RELEASE for cuts, refs, publication, successor identity and evidence; REFERENCE_FRAME, FOUNDATIONS §§2 and 4 and ACTIVATION §§2–3 for evaluation, acquisition and result law; standards/frames for verbatim task-specific owning sections, including bootstrap, with no determination ownership; and optional EXECUTIVE_BASELINE for Executive/Worker/Reviewer, technical triage and disposition, with testing frames in ASSURANCE.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 644,
          "quote": "- `SPEC_METHOD.md`: constitutional chain, triage, requirements,\n  construction, and proportional delivery (section 8);\n- `ACTIVATION.md`: the bounded construction step and proportionality;\n- `ASSURANCE.md`: testing;\n- `TICKETS.md`: work carriers, fields, states, execution contract, test\n  authority, and projection;\n- `RELEASE.md`: immutable cuts, qualified transport refs, publication,\n  successor identity, and release evidence;\n- `REFERENCE_FRAME.md`, `FOUNDATIONS.md` sections 2 and 4 (Results) and\n  `ACTIVATION.md` sections 2 and 3: bounded evaluation, acquisition and\n  result law;",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/GETTING_STARTED.md#Using%20STDO%2FOwning%20References",
          "start_line": 634
        }
      ],
      "key": "guide_owning_references",
      "label": "Guide owning-reference index"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Product Basis Selection is a read-only procedure preceding every STDO workflow skill. It selects and verifies one Product basis and grants no mutation, execution, review, disposition, installation or continuation authority.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 5,
          "quote": "Use this read-only procedure before every STDO workflow skill. It selects and\nverifies one Product basis; it grants no mutation, execution, review,\ndisposition, installation, or continuation authority.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/PRODUCT_BASIS.md#Product%20Basis%20Selection",
          "start_line": 3
        }
      ],
      "key": "product_basis_selection",
      "label": "Product Basis Selection"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["The selected basis has verified."],
      "definition": "Member acquisition resolves a package-relative member path and, where needed, its heading anchor through the same immutable basis. Membership, bytes, installation location and anchors are checked independently of semantic fidelity and task sufficiency.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 47,
          "quote": "After the selected basis has verified, resolve each required member through\nthat same immutable basis. A route consists of the member's package-relative\npath and, where needed, a heading anchor within it.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/PRODUCT_BASIS.md#Product%20Basis%20Selection%2FRead%20A%20Member%20From%20That%20Basis",
          "start_line": 45
        }
      ],
      "key": "verified_member_acquisition",
      "label": "Verified member acquisition"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Refresh is a read-only context projection reloading one complete registry entry from exactly one selected STDO basis. An entry is a declared bundle, owning member or task frame; projection creates no partial constitution.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 5,
          "quote": "Reload one complete registry entry from exactly one selected STDO basis. An\nentry is a declared bundle, owning member or task frame of this method. This is a read-only context\nprojection; it does not create a partial constitution.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/REFRESH.md#STDO%20Refresh%20Procedure",
          "start_line": 3
        }
      ],
      "key": "refresh_projection",
      "label": "STDO Refresh Procedure"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Ordered registry mappings are: frame → REFERENCE_FRAME.md; FOUNDATIONS.md §§2,4; ACTIVATION.md §§1–4,7; EVALUATION.md §7. frame-baseline → EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md; ASSURANCE.md §§7–13; EVALUATION.md §4. spec → SPEC_METHOD.md; ACTIVATION.md; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md; ASSURANCE.md; EVALUATION.md; TICKETS.md; FOUNDATIONS.md §§2,3; PROFILES.md §§2,3. design → DESIGN_MODULE.md; ASSURANCE.md §§14–16; ACTIVATION.md §§1,4,6; SPEC_METHOD.md §2; FOUNDATIONS.md §4. odd → ODD.md. ux → UX.md; TICKETS.md §3; PROFILES.md §2. writing → WRITING_GUIDE.md. posting → POSTING_GUIDE.md; SPEC_METHOD.md §6. ticket → TICKETS.md; ACTIVATION.md §1; SPEC_METHOD.md §§3,7. release → RELEASE.md; FOUNDATIONS.md §§1,2; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §4; EVALUATION.md §5. identity → IDENTITY.md; RELEASE.md §§1,3,8; DESIGN_MODULE.md §12. world → WORLD_MODEL.md; FOUNDATIONS.md §3. glossary → GLOSSARY.md; PROFILES.md §2. calculus → AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md. traversal → TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md; AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md §8. library → README.md; PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md §§4,12; RELEASE.md §§3,4. These identify acquisition targets, not verified contents.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 44,
          "quote": "| `frame` | `REFERENCE_FRAME.md`; `FOUNDATIONS.md` §2 and §4; `ACTIVATION.md` §1 to §4 and §7; `EVALUATION.md` §7 |\n| `frame-baseline` | `EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md`; `ASSURANCE.md` §7 to §13; `EVALUATION.md` §4 |\n| `spec` | `SPEC_METHOD.md`; `ACTIVATION.md`; `PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md`; `ASSURANCE.md`; `EVALUATION.md`; `TICKETS.md`; `FOUNDATIONS.md` §2 and §3; `PROFILES.md` §2 and §3 |\n| `design` | `DESIGN_MODULE.md`; `ASSURANCE.md` §14 to §16; `ACTIVATION.md` §1, §4 and §6; `SPEC_METHOD.md` §2; `FOUNDATIONS.md` §4 |\n| `odd` | `ODD.md` |\n| `ux` | `UX.md`; `TICKETS.md` §3; `PROFILES.md` §2 |\n| `writing` | `WRITING_GUIDE.md` |\n| `posting` | `POSTING_GUIDE.md`; `SPEC_METHOD.md` §6 |\n| `ticket` | `TICKETS.md`; `ACTIVATION.md` §1; `SPEC_METHOD.md` §3 and §7 |\n| `release` | `RELEASE.md`; `FOUNDATIONS.md` §1 and §2; `PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md` §4; `EVALUATION.md` §5 |\n| `identity` | `IDENTITY.md`; `RELEASE.md` §1, §3 and §8; `DESIGN_MODULE.md` §12 |\n| `world` | `WORLD_MODEL.md`; `FOUNDATIONS.md` §3 |\n| `glossary` | `GLOSSARY.md`; `PROFILES.md` §2 |\n| `calculus` | `AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md` |\n| `traversal` | `TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE.md`; `AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md` §8 |\n| `library` | `README.md`; `PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md` §4 and §12; `RELEASE.md` §3 and §4 |",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/REFRESH.md#STDO%20Refresh%20Procedure%2FRegistry",
          "start_line": 29
        }
      ],
      "key": "refresh_bundle_registry",
      "label": "Refresh bundle registry"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "owner:<member> identifies one owning standards member by exact filename without .md. Task names map to frames/<suffix>.md for suffixes rf-task-a, rf-task-b, ac-task-a, traversal-task-f, eb-task-d, dm-task-d, configuration, binding, stale-summary, bootstrap, acceptance-release, and member-build-assess. Existing bundle names remain available.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 53,
          "quote": "The bundle names above remain available. `owner:<member>` selects one owning\nmember, using its exact filename without `.md`, such as\n`owner:FOUNDATIONS`, `owner:ACTIVATION` or `owner:WORLD_MODEL`. Accept only a\nmember listed in the verified standards inventory; the local\n[method entry](../../../standards/README.md) locates its scope. A full owner\nread has its own acquisition cost; select a task entry when it is sufficient.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/REFRESH.md#STDO%20Refresh%20Procedure%2FOwner%20And%20Task%20Entries",
          "start_line": 48
        },
        {
          "end_line": 68,
          "quote": "| `task:rf-task-a` | `frames/rf-task-a.md` |\n| `task:rf-task-b` | `frames/rf-task-b.md` |\n| `task:ac-task-a` | `frames/ac-task-a.md` |\n| `task:traversal-task-f` | `frames/traversal-task-f.md` |\n| `task:eb-task-d` | `frames/eb-task-d.md` |\n| `task:dm-task-d` | `frames/dm-task-d.md` |\n| `task:configuration` | `frames/configuration.md` |\n| `task:binding` | `frames/binding.md` |\n| `task:stale-summary` | `frames/stale-summary.md` |\n| `task:bootstrap` | `frames/bootstrap.md` |\n| `task:acceptance-release` | `frames/acceptance-release.md` |\n| `task:member-build-assess` | `frames/member-build-assess.md` |",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/references/REFRESH.md#STDO%20Refresh%20Procedure%2FOwner%20And%20Task%20Entries",
          "start_line": 57
        }
      ],
      "key": "refresh_owner_task_entries",
      "label": "Refresh owner and task entries"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["The request says stdo help or explicitly concerns entering or operating an STDO-governed project."],
      "definition": "stdo-help explains or establishes the next lawful STDO step through practical help from the project's exact selected basis. It routes attention and does not replace method or Product authority.",
      "exceptions": ["Generic non-STDO help is outside its invocation scope."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3,
          "quote": "description: Explain or establish the next lawful STDO step. Use when a user says stdo help or explicitly asks how to enter or operate an STDO-governed project. Do not invoke for generic non-STDO help.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-help/SKILL.md#preamble",
          "start_line": 3
        },
        {
          "end_line": 9,
          "quote": "Give practical help from the project's exact selected basis. This skill routes\nattention; it does not replace method or Product authority.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-help/SKILL.md#STDO%20Help",
          "start_line": 8
        }
      ],
      "key": "stdo_help",
      "label": "STDO Help"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["The request says stdo review or explicitly concerns an STDO-governed candidate, release claim, qualification claim or governed boundary."],
      "definition": "stdo-review independently evaluates one exact claim or candidate as Reviewer and returns a closed technical result. It is read-only and does not repair, assign Product priority, apply disposition or activate next work.",
      "exceptions": ["Generic review is outside its invocation scope."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3,
          "quote": "description: Independently evaluate one exact STDO-governed candidate and return a closed technical result. Use when a user says stdo review or explicitly asks to review an STDO-governed candidate, release claim, qualification claim, or governed boundary. Do not invoke for generic review.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-review/SKILL.md#preamble",
          "start_line": 3
        },
        {
          "end_line": 9,
          "quote": "Act only as Reviewer for one exact claim. Review is read-only. It does not\nrepair, assign Product priority, apply disposition, or activate the next work.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-review/SKILL.md#STDO%20Review",
          "start_line": 8
        }
      ],
      "key": "stdo_review",
      "label": "STDO Review"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The review projection names five core result values: satisfied, falsified, indeterminate, out_of_frame and invalid_basis. They remain distinct from technical triage and Product disposition.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 79,
          "quote": "- `satisfied`: no finding; triage is `not_applicable`;\n- `falsified`: findings carry complete triage or explicit field-level\n  indeterminate values;\n- `indeterminate` or `out_of_frame`: return the unresolved triage and basis;\n  and\n- `invalid_basis`: triage is `not_applicable`; return the basis re-entry.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-review/SKILL.md#STDO%20Review%2FEvaluate",
          "start_line": 74
        }
      ],
      "key": "review_result_domain",
      "label": "Review result domain"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["The request says stdo status or explicitly requests progress, blockers, monitoring or triage help for an STDO-governed project."],
      "definition": "stdo-status produces evidence-backed read-only Product/work delivery status and bounded triage candidates from Product-owned authority and evidence. The shell stdo status command instead reports installed-basis integrity.",
      "exceptions": ["Generic status is outside its invocation scope."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3,
          "quote": "description: Produce an evidence-backed read-only STDO project status and bounded triage candidates. Use when a user says stdo status or explicitly asks for progress, blockers, monitoring, or triage help in an STDO-governed project. Do not invoke for generic status.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-status/SKILL.md#preamble",
          "start_line": 3
        },
        {
          "end_line": 10,
          "quote": "Report Product and work truth without changing it. The shell command `stdo\nstatus` reports installed-basis integrity; this skill reports project delivery\nstate from Product-owned authority and evidence.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-status/SKILL.md#STDO%20Status",
          "start_line": 8
        }
      ],
      "key": "stdo_status",
      "label": "STDO Status"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["The request says stdo ticket or explicitly requests ticketing, opening or updating an STDO-governed request, bug, failed test, finding or release issue."],
      "definition": "stdo-ticket turns intake into one durable governed work carrier without starting implementation.",
      "exceptions": ["Read-only classification is outside its invocation scope."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3,
          "quote": "description: Create or update one governed STDO work item. Use when a user says stdo ticket or explicitly asks to ticket, open, or update an STDO-governed request, bug, failed test, finding, or release issue. Do not invoke for read-only classification.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-ticket/SKILL.md#preamble",
          "start_line": 3
        },
        {
          "end_line": 8,
          "quote": "Turn an intake into one durable work carrier without starting implementation.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-ticket/SKILL.md#STDO%20Ticket",
          "start_line": 8
        }
      ],
      "key": "stdo_ticket",
      "label": "STDO Ticket"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["The request says stdo work or explicitly requests requirements, design, code or test work under an STDO-governed basis."],
      "definition": "stdo-work executes one admitted work item through its lawful re-entry point and delivers the smallest causally closed change authorized by one exact work basis. The admitted re-entry point decides where work begins.",
      "exceptions": ["Generic non-STDO development is outside its invocation scope."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3,
          "quote": "description: Execute one admitted STDO work item through its lawful re-entry point. Use when a user says stdo work or explicitly asks to perform requirements, design, code, or test work under an STDO-governed basis. Do not invoke for generic non-STDO development.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/plugins/spec/skills/stdo-work/SKILL.md#preamble",
          "start_line": 3
        },
        {
          "end_line": 9,
          "quote": "Deliver the smallest causally closed change authorized by one exact work basis.\nThe admitted re-entry point decides where work begins.",
