    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A transition is one step's bounded change from current to next state. Work fitting one activation is one transition; work exceeding it is refined into bounded transitions under the declared refinement law.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 138,
          "quote": "A transition is a bounded change from the current state to a next state,\ncarried out by one step. Where the work exceeds one activation's capacity,\nthe outer transformation towards the destination is refined into a series\nof bounded transitions under §4 Refinement, each carried out by its own\nstep; work that fits one activation is a single transition.",
