    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The construction relation binds current state A and destination predicate Z, selects work, composes steps, corrects discrepancies and grounds completion claims. Its three subject accounts are specification of required conditions, observations of what holds, and causal/predictive explanation of possible action effects. Strategy arranges admissible construction and assurance within resources; a composition boundary passes one step's output into the next starting state and differs from a categorical join. Feedback observes, compares, diagnoses, selects an authorized response, acts and observes again; homeostasis is correction toward required conditions without a convergence or adequacy guarantee.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 206,
          "quote": "This subsection states the construction relation for this corpus: how a\nselected construction binds its current state and destination, chooses\nits work, composes its steps, corrects itself and claims completion. This\nsection owns that relation. ACTIVATION §2 to §7, EVALUATION §1,\nSPEC_METHOD §4 and §8, EXECUTIVE_BASELINE and ODD apply it through their\nlocal bindings; none creates a competing determination (P6).",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FConstruction%20relation",
