    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The execution unit is the smallest coherent causal dependency cone able to deliver working behaviour while preserving every affected governing relation. It need not align with a function, file, module, ticket field or design document. It is the seed set called Z for context construction in ACTIVATION §2, distinct in usage from construction's destination predicate Z.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 400,
          "quote": "The execution unit is the smallest coherent causal dependency cone capable\nof delivering working behaviour while preserving every affected governing\nrelation. It need not coincide with one function, file, module, ticket\nfield or design document (P0, P4b). A seam whose far side can causally affect,\nor be affected by, the action is inside the cone unless the basis\nestablishes that it cannot participate. Unrelated incompleteness outside\nthe cone is recorded as repricing input and does not block the bounded\nclaim. The cone is the seed set Z of §2; the context is its projection.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/ACTIVATION.md#ACTIVATION%2F1.%20The%20step%2FExecution%20unit",
