      "key": "execution_unit",
      "label": "Execution unit"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Execution-contract drafting and admission are distinct relations. Contracts carry at least drafted, admitted, rejected and superseded states. Admission validates a contract against its cited outcome, prerequisite or experiment basis; it does not admit that underlying basis.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 408,
          "quote": "Drafting a step's contract and admitting it are distinct relations, even\ninside one invocation that drafts, validates, admits and executes; no\nseparate turn, carrier or approval ceremony is implied by the distinction.\nA contract carries at minimum the states drafted, admitted, rejected and\nsuperseded ([TICKETS §5](TICKETS.md#execution-contract-admission)).",
