      "label": "Execution-contract admission"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Applicability evaluates the owning predicate that an obligation applies to an exact subject, using sufficient basis-bound facts. Exclusion is the state of an obligation following falsified applicability, not a result of that obligation's own evaluation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
