    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A configuration allocates task responsibilities and information exchanges to frames across the work; activation binds actors to frames. An active frame configuration is the portion used for one evaluation or decision. A coordinator, where selected, manages delivery across tasks from bounded closed results. The optional Executive configuration assigns construction to Worker/Writer, assessment to Reviewer, and longer-term outcome, next-work selection and granted disposition to a non-mutating Executive; it is not the method default.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
