      "key": "applicability_result_and_coverage_law",
      "statement": "Owning evaluation/scope predicates determine obligations from sufficient basis-bound facts. True applicability is satisfied and requires evaluation/result; false is falsified with its basis-bound counterexample and excludes only that obligation under cited authority. Missing/ambiguous premise is indeterminate, or out_of_frame if it needs an undeclared relation, never falsified. Exclusion has no obligation result/core value, removes only that obligation from conjunction coverage and waives no acceptance criterion; unresolved applicability remains in coverage and withholds dependent claim until evidence/owner decision resolves it. Owner-declared disjunction including non-application may be satisfied by exclusion, but that satisfaction belongs only to the disjunction, never the obligation-holds predicate. Frame/tool/family availability alone triggers no activation. Residual semantic applicability judgment retains judgment/evidence identity rather than masquerading as computation. Missing, stale, wrong-subject/basis or incapable required results cannot satisfy conjunction; other applicable constraints remain even when detected by only one evaluation. Finite declared qualification fixtures must distinguish true/false/unknown premises, missing/wrong-subject results and sufficient positive result; always-skip/always-activate rules fail those distinct expectations. Members/profiles/projects reuse this exclusion owner rather than redefining it.",
